WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
Chesapeake Bay, USA.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.510
Its watershed spans six states
and the District of Columbia.

3
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.410
Every summer, parts of the bay hold less
than 2 milligrams of dissolved oxygen

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:12.550
per litre.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.110
Too little for fish and shellfish.

6
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.450
Dead zones.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.110
And much of the cause starts on land.

8
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.970
How can a farm field suffocate a bay?

9
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.230
Do factories pump in hot water?

10
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.190
Do ships churn up mud?

11
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.940
In this mission, you'll
meet the stakeholders.

12
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:33.270
In 2010, the EPA put the
bay on a pollution diet.

13
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.070
Then you'll see what irrigation can
do to soils in hot, dry regions.

14
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.190
Your mission: explain how a
farm field can suffocate a bay.
